list.item:
The eLiebermann Lawcodes Database presents the laws clause by clause, according to Liebermann’s own editorial divisions and in his order. It contains:


the Old English, Latin or French text as Liebermann prints it, labelled by manuscript;

Liebermann’s German translation, with an English rendering of it;

the texts and translations of later editors (see Rights below);

Liebermann’s textual notes and commentary, with his references to other works and manuscripts explained;

a new subject index of offences, persons, institutions and places;

cross-references between clauses, from Liebermann and from later scholars, each with its source and linked in both directions;

continuous reading texts of the Instituta Cnuti and the Consiliatio Cnuti, which Liebermann prints only in pieces beside their sources.

The eLiebermann Legal Dictionary is a digital edition of Liebermann’s Wörterbuch (volume II, part 1), the dictionary of the Old English, Latin and French words of the laws. It contains:


Liebermann’s abbreviations and grammatical terms, expanded and translated;

his sigla for law codes and manuscripts, explained;

a link from every law he cites to the clause in the Lawcodes Database, with the word marked;

links to the works he cites;

links to the corresponding entries in Bosworth–Toller and the Dictionary of Old English (still being checked).
